  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070857/assets/51bf87385bc52632a0bf722d5672047e79afc8ea0556dabda3257c9ebd1e91a3.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x.$\n\n- Finally, translate it by $3$ units **down** to give $y=-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x-3$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x-3.$",
